  "user_request": "The municipal bus and metro union just announced a 3-day total transport strike from Wednesday to Friday (Tuesday 18:00). Without buses, my commute from home to the High-Performance Center (HPC) increases from 25 to 60 minutes (by bike/foot), and from the HPC to the university campus increases from 30 to 65 minutes. Since training is my top priority, I cannot afford to spend 3 hours a day commuting back and forth between the HPC and campus, nor can I cut into my 8 hours of sleep. Please reorganise Wednesday to Friday: drop non-mandatory campus classes to stay near the HPC/home for rest and study, ask my group project teammates to switch Thursday's meeting to a video call, adjust all morning commute start times (shifting sleep slightly earlier if needed to maintain 8 hours), and let me know what to confirm with others."
}
